h the  67 lines with east jerusalem as its  capital for the palestinian leadership  however such words are just that words  they see this entire summit in this  place as an undermining of their cause  for sovereignty and independence  the palestinian prime minister focused  on what was happening inside israel  arab normalization meetings without  ending the israeli occupation of  palestine are just an illusion a mirage  and a free reward for israel  palestinian president meanwhile had his  own diplomacy to conduct welcoming  jordan's king abdullah to ramallah on a  mission to calm tensions ahead of  ramadan  harry fawcett al-jazeera southern israel  ibrahim has more on reaction to the  negev summit from ramallah in the west  bank  there is a lot of criticism by  palestinian officials that the way the  americans and some arab leaders are  dealing with this whole issue  palestinian officials have been saying  over the past few months even that we  want to engage in a political process  that ends the israeli occupation they're  refusing any talks of better living  conditions of diffusing tension while  the palestinians are still living and  feeling the brunt and the pain of being  under the israeli occupation there's a  lot of talk in the street as well  they're saying that the world is dealing  with double standards when it comes to  the palestinian we see them sympathizing  with ukrainians as they are now under  the russian occupation but turning a  blind eye when it comes to palestinians  who have been living under the israeli  occupation for decades so there's a lot  of disappointment amongst politicians  and people in the street asking to be a  part of the dialogue asking the world to  impose sanctions on israel to end its  occupation we're seeing that they're  getting some positive signs from jordan  instead of the jordanian being in the  summit we hear that they declined the  invitation and the jordanian king has  decided to meet with president abbas the  talks 